{"author":{"id":"6d85cf2fcebaeefd8c5c528f2d5f5f98f26ce3275422d0dc5f7c0fd596f9f59f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792162632,"nonce":"6LRGv+8BRXbmicg//WhLnH4HMWQ=","title":"Expose a cheap native version check for string signals","message":"SignalString.get() on the Haxe side (ashui) decodes a fresh Haxe String\non every read, even when the native value hasn't changed: a native UTF-8\ncopy plus a Haxe-side decode, per read. Ashui's own issue (git-bug 2059910\nin the ashui repo) tracks the fix: cache the decoded string, keyed by a\ncheap revision number, and only redo the decode when that number changes.\n\nAdded hl_blinc_signal_string_version, wrapping the new\nSignal::version() (git-bug b106ffb4a5af0f65dd5358aa458db6c4b3972c09c1204fd876e673d52937bfff\nin Blinc). Untracked: callers pair it with the existing\nblinc_signal_touch to keep registering the dependency.","files":null}]}